What does “the Bean” refer to in Chicago?

Cloud Gate is a public artwork created by Anish Kapoor, a British artist of Indian origin, and serves as the focal point of AT&T Plaza in Millennium Park, located in Chicago’s Loop district. The piece and the plaza sit atop the Park Grill, nestled between the Chase Promenade and the McCormick Tribune Plaza & Ice Rink. Built from 2004 to 2006, the sculpture earned the nickname “the Bean” due to its curved, bean‑like form—a moniker Kapoor initially rejected but later embraced. It consists of 168 stainless‑steel plates welded together, producing a seamless, mirror‑like surface. The work measures roughly 33 × 66 × 42 feet (10 × 20 × 13 m) and weighs about 110 short tons (≈100 t or 98 long tons).

